00:33:52.340 --> 00:33:53.560
I love cleaning windows.
我很喜欢擦窗户。

797
00:33:53.700 --> 00:33:54.200
I don't mind it.
我不介意。

798
00:33:54.340 --> 00:33:54.920
You know why?
你知道为什么吗？

799
00:33:54.920 --> 00:33:56.420
It's like an immediate result.
因为见效快。

800
00:33:56.680 --> 00:33:57.740
I think that's what I like.
我想这就是我喜欢的原因。

801
00:33:57.920 --> 00:34:00.100
And lastly, cleaning the gutters.
最后是清理排水槽。

802
00:34:00.640 --> 00:34:01.840
I don't want to clean the gutters.
我不想清理排水槽。

803
00:34:01.960 --> 00:34:02.900
Josh cleans the gutters.
乔希去清理排水槽。

804
00:34:03.020 --> 00:34:04.060
I don't want to clean the gutters.
我不想清理排水槽。

805
00:34:04.400 --> 00:34:07.000
I also can't reach, even on our tallest ladder.
而且我也够不着，哪怕踩着家里最高的人字梯也不行。

806
00:34:07.640 --> 00:34:07.880
Sure.
当然。

807
00:34:08.080 --> 00:34:10.940
It's so interesting that that one was included.
真有意思，那个居然被列进去了。

808
00:34:11.240 --> 00:34:11.820
You know what?
你知道吗？

809
00:34:11.900 --> 00:34:13.300
They didn't include on that liSt.
他们没把这个列在清单上。

810
00:34:13.440 --> 00:34:18.160
Maybe this just falls under laundry, but this would be real high on my list of things I hate doing.
也许这应该算在洗衣服里面，但这绝对会在我最讨厌做的事情里名列前茅。

811
00:34:18.660 --> 00:34:19.100
Sheets.
床单。

812
00:34:19.380 --> 00:34:19.700
Yeah.
对。

813
00:34:19.700 --> 00:34:22.860
Putting sheets on a bed, making a bed from scratch.
给床套床单，从头铺一张床。

814
00:34:22.860 --> 00:34:25.320
I don't mind making a bed that already has covers on it.
我不介意整理一张已经铺好被罩的床。

815
00:34:25.420 --> 00:34:25.600
Yeah.
对。

816
00:34:25.880 --> 00:34:27.020
I don't mind that.
我不介意那个。

817
00:34:27.420 --> 00:34:27.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

818
00:34:27.820 --> 00:34:28.420
I don't mind.
我不介意。

819
00:34:28.600 --> 00:34:30.440
Like, the fitted sheet doesn't bother me.
比如，装床笠对我来说不是问题。

820
00:34:31.080 --> 00:34:36.300
I'm very lucky because I feel like Lee and I, we balance each other.
我很幸运，因为我觉得我和莉互补。

821
00:34:36.420 --> 00:34:36.600
Yes.
对。

822
00:34:36.600 --> 00:34:38.540
The things I hate, he doesn't mind.
我讨厌的事，他不介意。

823
00:34:38.760 --> 00:34:38.900
Yeah.
对。

824
00:34:39.140 --> 00:34:42.160
If we're going to clean up the house, he does all the vacuuming.
如果要打扫房子，吸尘全归他包了。

825
00:34:42.240 --> 00:34:43.700
He just, like, gets on it.
他就是那种二话不说直接开干的人。

826
00:34:43.840 --> 00:34:46.100
And I'm happy to do the bathrooMs.
而我很乐意去打扫浴室。

827
00:34:46.540 --> 00:34:47.280
It's interesting.
这挺有意思的。

828
00:34:47.580 --> 00:34:47.700
Yeah.
是啊。

829
00:34:47.700 --> 00:34:48.740
We never talked about it.
我们从来没商量过。

830
00:34:48.800 --> 00:34:49.580
It just sort of happened.
就是自然而然地分工了。

831
00:34:49.640 --> 00:34:50.480
Same with Josh and I.
我和乔希也是一样。

832
00:34:50.540 --> 00:34:52.760
We just sort of found our strengths or something.
我们只是差不多找到了各自擅长的事。

833
00:34:52.900 --> 00:34:52.980
Yeah.
对。

834
00:34:52.980 --> 00:34:54.100
We just leaned into them.
我们顺其自然地发挥了各自的优势。

835
00:34:54.300 --> 00:34:54.720
Exactly.
没错。

836
00:34:55.040 --> 00:35:00.660
Well, this cold open is going to end with Meredith trotting away, very excited to clean some toilets.
好了，这个冷开场最后会以梅雷迪思小跑着离开、兴高采烈地去刷马桶结束。

837
00:35:00.920 --> 00:35:06.200
Then we're going to zoom in on a little rat that's walking around Dwight and Jim's desks.
然后镜头会拉近到一只在德怀特和吉姆办公桌周围走来走去的小老鼠身上。

838
00:35:06.640 --> 00:35:08.900
This rat was, of course, from Bob Dunn's.
这只老鼠当然是来自鲍勃·邓恩动物租赁公司。

839
00:35:09.420 --> 00:35:10.980
Where do they keep all these animals?
他们把所有这些动物都养在哪里？

840
00:35:11.300 --> 00:35:14.320
They have dogs, cats, porcupines, rats, squirrels.
他们有狗、猫、豪猪、老鼠、松鼠。

841
00:35:14.380 --> 00:35:15.060
Where are they?
它们都在哪儿？

842
00:35:15.440 --> 00:35:16.120
I'd like to think.
我宁愿相信。

843
00:35:16.120 --> 00:35:16.900
Do they live together?
它们住在一起吗？

844
00:35:17.100 --> 00:35:18.120
Bob Dunn has a farm.
鲍勃·邓恩有个农场。

845
00:35:18.280 --> 00:35:19.200
That's what I'd like to think.
我宁愿这么想。

846
00:35:19.380 --> 00:35:19.900
I don't know.
我不知道。

847
00:35:19.980 --> 00:35:21.140
It's so interesting to me.
我对这个太感兴趣了。

848
00:35:21.280 --> 00:35:25.800
Anyway, Steve Burgess said he thinks that the rat cost about $200 a day.
不管怎样，史蒂夫·伯吉斯说他觉得这只老鼠一天的费用大约是200美元。

849
00:35:26.380 --> 00:35:28.160
We had to hire it for two days.
我们不得不雇了两天。

850
00:35:28.320 --> 00:35:30.860
It needed its training day and a shooting day.
它需要一个训练日和一个拍摄日。

851
00:35:31.500 --> 00:35:34.720
And we also had to pay for the trainer plus transportation.
我们还得支付驯兽师和交通费用。

852
00:35:34.720 --> 00:35:39.820
So, in the end, it was about $1,500 to get that shot of the rat.
所以最后为了拍那个老鼠镜头，大约花了1500美元。

853
00:35:39.940 --> 00:35:40.560
That rat shot.
那个老鼠镜头。

854
00:35:40.780 --> 00:35:41.120
In the trash.
结果进了垃圾桶。

855
00:35:41.320 --> 00:35:47.100
Well, you know, there was part of me when we saw that little rat that really wanted Aaron or Daryl to have a name for it.
嗯，你知道的，当我们看到那只小老鼠时，我心里有一部分真的很希望亚伦或达里尔给它起个名字。

856
00:35:47.140 --> 00:35:49.460
Because we know they've been feeding mice for years.
因为我们知道他们喂老鼠好多年了。

857
00:35:49.460 --> 00:35:50.700
Maybe they know this dude.
也许他们认识这家伙。

858
00:35:51.020 --> 00:35:51.340
Yes.
是的。

859
00:35:51.340 --> 00:35:53.480
Maybe Daryl has a little top hat for it.
也许达里尔为它准备了一顶小礼帽。

860
00:35:53.580 --> 00:35:53.780
Yeah.
对。

861
00:35:54.040 --> 00:35:55.060
Oh, that would have been cute.
哦，那一定很可爱。

862
00:35:55.360 --> 00:35:56.460
Well, the show is going to open.
好了，剧集要开始了。

863
00:35:56.600 --> 00:35:57.640
We're at Jim and Pam's house.
我们在吉姆和帕姆的家里。

864
00:35:57.660 --> 00:35:58.820
They're loading up the car.
他们正在往车上装东西。

865
00:35:58.820 --> 00:36:00.740
Cece's playing in the front yard.
西西在前院玩耍。

866
00:36:00.960 --> 00:36:03.300
Looks like she has her little, like, snuggle blanket on her head.
看起来她头上盖着她那条像小毯子一样的东西。

867
00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:06.320
She has the same little lovey that my kids used.
她用的安抚毛毯和我孩子们用的一模一样。

868
00:36:06.560 --> 00:36:07.120
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

869
00:36:07.160 --> 00:36:07.500
Yeah.
是啊。

870
00:36:07.720 --> 00:36:08.300
So cute.
太可爱了。

871
00:36:08.560 --> 00:36:08.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

872
00:36:09.180 --> 00:36:13.760
Well, per the call sheet, this day, the high was 101 degrees.
好吧，根据通告单，这一天的最高气温是101华氏度。

873
00:36:14.060 --> 00:36:15.080
It was Tuesday.
那天是星期二。

874
00:36:15.500 --> 00:36:18.760
We also had a table read this day for Andy's Ancestry.
我们这一天还要为《安迪的身世》进行剧本围读。

875
00:36:18.760 --> 00:36:23.220
And I thought you might like to have a little get-to-know-your-cast-and-crew moment.
我想你可能会喜欢来一段“了解你的演职人员”的环节。

876
00:36:23.640 --> 00:36:24.620
Oh, all right.
哦，好的。

877
00:36:24.700 --> 00:36:25.240
Sounds good.
听起来不错。

878
00:36:25.420 --> 00:36:26.980
I have two for this episode.
我为这一集准备了两个。

879
00:36:27.420 --> 00:36:32.420
First one up was Edward Nielsen III from our camera and electrical department.
首先登场的是我们摄影和灯光部门的爱德华·尼尔森三世。

880
00:36:32.620 --> 00:36:35.180
Here are things you didn't know about Ed Nielsen.
以下是你所不知道的关于埃德·尼尔森的事情。

881
00:36:35.540 --> 00:36:36.460
It says,
上面写着，

882
00:36:37.040 --> 00:36:38.220
Oh, where to begin?
哦，从何说起呢？

883
00:36:38.560 --> 00:36:39.600
Dot, dot, dot.
点，点，点。

884
00:36:40.120 --> 00:36:40.640
Dot.
点。

885
00:36:41.380 --> 00:36:41.960
Four dots.
四个点。

886
00:36:42.580 --> 00:36:44.440
Ed speaks orcish.
埃德会说兽人语。

887
00:36:44.860 --> 00:36:47.160
Misses having no responsibility in his childhood
怀念童年时无忧无虑的日子

888
00:36:47.160 --> 00:36:49.500
and looks forward to doing nothing on the weekends.
并且期待在周末无所事事。

889
00:36:49.760 --> 00:36:53.760
When asked about time travel, he said it is BS and for Trekkies.
当被问及时间旅行时，他说那是无稽之谈，是给《星际迷航》迷准备的。

890
00:36:55.840 --> 00:36:58.140
And, of course, my folks that love Lord of the Rings,
当然，我那些喜欢《指环王》的朋友们，

891
00:36:58.280 --> 00:37:00.980
you know orcish is the primary language of the orcs.
你们知道兽人语是兽人的主要语言。

892
00:37:01.360 --> 00:37:02.260
Oh, I didn't know that.
哦，我不知道这个。

893
00:37:02.260 --> 00:37:03.940
It is the main language of the horde.
它是部落的主要语言。

894
00:37:04.180 --> 00:37:05.180
So it's made up.
所以它是虚构的。

895
00:37:05.540 --> 00:37:06.660
It's a made-up language.
这是一门虚构的语言。

896
00:37:07.500 --> 00:37:07.940
Oh.
哦。

897
00:37:08.560 --> 00:37:11.340
I didn't know it when you said it.
你刚才说的时候我并不知道。

898
00:37:11.460 --> 00:37:11.800
Okay.
好吧。

899
00:37:11.980 --> 00:37:13.920
You had a blank look on your face.
你当时一脸茫然。

900
00:37:13.920 --> 00:37:18.560
I was like, oh, this must be some sort of Nordic language.
我想，哦，这肯定是什么北欧语言吧。

901
00:37:18.600 --> 00:37:20.120
I didn't know what it was.
我不知道那是什么。

902
00:37:20.260 --> 00:37:21.540
I was like, so impressive.
我当时就觉得，太让人惊艳了。

903
00:37:21.540 --> 00:37:22.840
I didn't know he spoke that.
我都不知道他会说那种话。

904
00:37:23.620 --> 00:37:25.760
I would have read that and then gone up to him and be like,
我要是读到那个，然后走过去对他说，

905
00:37:25.860 --> 00:37:26.980
oh, my God, you speak this.
天哪，你会说这个。

906
00:37:27.060 --> 00:37:27.800
Where is it from?
这是哪里来的？

907
00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:28.960
What is orcish?
什么是兽人语？

908
00:37:29.120 --> 00:37:29.420
Yes.
是的。

909
00:37:29.660 --> 00:37:33.220
I'll have you know, Angela, we shot this scene first up in the day.
安吉拉，我得告诉你，我们这天一早先拍了这场戏。

910
00:37:33.360 --> 00:37:35.440
It was very, very early to avoid the heat.
为了避暑，当时真的非常非常早。

911
00:37:35.740 --> 00:37:37.740
We're going to see Jim in a talking head.
我们接下来会看到吉姆的单人访谈。

912
00:37:37.740 --> 00:37:39.000
He's all dressed up.
他盛装打扮了一番。

913
00:37:39.160 --> 00:37:40.080
So is Pam.
帕姆也是。

914
00:37:40.380 --> 00:37:44.640
He explains they are going to Roy's wedding at 8 a.m.
他解释说他们要在早上8点去参加罗伊的婚礼。

915
00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:45.200
Yeah.
是啊。

916
00:37:45.460 --> 00:37:47.980
We got a fan mail flurry about this, Ange.
安吉，我们为此收到了雪片般飞来的粉丝来信。

917
00:37:48.140 --> 00:37:48.600
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

918
00:37:49.140 --> 00:37:52.840
People want to know, why would Pam and Jim go to Roy's wedding?
大家都在问，帕姆和吉姆为什么会去参加罗伊的婚礼？

919
00:37:53.140 --> 00:37:55.320
Why would they even be invited?
他们怎么会收到邀请呢？

920
00:37:55.860 --> 00:37:56.300
Okay.
好吧。

921
00:37:56.500 --> 00:38:01.480
Well, there was a deleted storyline in last week's episode, New Guys, right?
嗯，上周的剧集《新人们》里有一条被删掉的故事情节，对吧？

922
00:38:01.540 --> 00:38:01.660
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

923
00:38:01.800 --> 00:38:04.280
And it sets up this Roy's wedding storyline.
正是这条线铺垫了罗伊婚礼的剧情。

924
00:38:04.280 --> 00:38:07.020
I really debated about sharing it last week, but then I thought,
我本来很纠结要不要在上周分享它，但后来我想，

925
00:38:07.200 --> 00:38:10.160
I don't want to give away any spoilers, so I'm going to share it this week.
我不想剧透，所以我打算这周再分享。

926
00:38:10.280 --> 00:38:10.500
Okay.
好的。

927
00:38:11.200 --> 00:38:15.820
Jim and Pam have a scene where they discuss what they're buying Roy for his upcoming wedding.
吉姆和帕姆有一场戏，他们讨论要给即将结婚的罗伊买什么礼物。

928
00:38:16.160 --> 00:38:16.600
Oh.
哦。

929
00:38:16.860 --> 00:38:17.080
Yeah.
是啊。

930
00:38:17.260 --> 00:38:18.580
And they're at their desk.
他们当时在办公桌前。

931
00:38:18.700 --> 00:38:20.780
They're looking at the wedding registry website.
在看婚礼礼物登记网站。

932
00:38:21.400 --> 00:38:23.960
And then there was a Pam talking head about it.
然后还有一个帕姆的单人访谈。

933
00:38:24.120 --> 00:38:24.740
Let's hear it.
我们听听看。

934
00:38:25.440 --> 00:38:28.600
Roy Anderson, my former fiancé, is getting married.
罗伊·安德森，我的前未婚夫，要结婚了。

935
00:38:30.120 --> 00:38:33.000
Unless his bride pulls what I'm sure they call Pam.
除非他的新娘也干出我确信他们会称之为“帕姆”的事。

936
00:38:33.700 --> 00:38:36.100
Or a, that bitch Pam.
或者说，那个贱人帕姆。

937
00:38:40.130 --> 00:38:45.970
And wait, there was a candy bag alt that was a must shoot, so you did say this to the camera.
等等，还有一个必须拍摄的糖果袋备用台词，所以你确实对着镜头说了这个。

938
00:38:46.250 --> 00:38:48.170
Here was an alt talking head.
这里有一个备用的单人访谈。

939
00:38:48.370 --> 00:38:52.950
Pam would have said, Roy Anderson, my former fiancé, is getting married.
帕姆本来说的是，罗伊·安德森，我的前未婚夫，要结婚了。

940
00:38:53.250 --> 00:38:57.610
What do you get for a man whose butt you've seen thousands of times?
送一个你屁股看过几千遍的男人什么礼物好呢？

941
00:38:57.870 --> 00:38:58.370
Okay.
好吧。

942
00:38:59.550 --> 00:39:02.450
And I zoomed in on the wedding registry website.
然后我把镜头推近到了婚礼礼物登记网站上。

943
00:39:02.530 --> 00:39:02.870
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

944
00:39:03.230 --> 00:39:06.290
They decide to get Roy a ladle, right?
他们决定送罗伊一个大汤勺，对吧？

945
00:39:06.530 --> 00:39:07.130
A ladle.
一个大汤勺。

946
00:39:07.130 --> 00:39:07.990
A fancy ladle.
一个精致的大汤勺。

947
00:39:08.230 --> 00:39:08.330
Okay.
好吧。

948
00:39:08.550 --> 00:39:10.250
And Pam's like, that doesn't seem like a lot.
然后帕姆说，这好像显得不太够。

949
00:39:10.390 --> 00:39:12.270
Jim's like, I don't know, get him the spoon too.
吉姆说，我不知道，连那把小勺子也送他吧。

950
00:39:13.330 --> 00:39:17.050
I looked, the ladle cost $174.
我查了一下，那个大汤勺要174美元。

951
00:39:18.170 --> 00:39:18.590
Whoa.
哇。

952
00:39:18.910 --> 00:39:19.270
Yeah.
对。

953
00:39:19.650 --> 00:39:22.370
Well, my question is, how big is this ladle?
不过我的问题是，这个大汤勺有多大？

954
00:39:22.470 --> 00:39:27.230
Because that gift that they're carrying out of Jim and Pam's house, that box is very large.
因为他们从吉姆和帕姆家抬出来的那个礼物，那个箱子非常大。

955
00:39:27.470 --> 00:39:27.630
I know.
我知道。

956
00:39:27.750 --> 00:39:28.410
I thought that too.
我也这么想。

957
00:39:28.510 --> 00:39:28.910
I'm like, what?
我在想，什么？

958
00:39:29.010 --> 00:39:30.750
Is that the ladle, the spoon, a platter?
那是大汤勺、汤匙，还是盘子？

959
00:39:30.750 --> 00:39:31.830
Actually, they went another way.
其实，他们选了别的东西。

960
00:39:32.070 --> 00:39:35.250
Well, we got another fan question from Kyle C.
好吧，我们收到了来自加利福尼亚州斯托克顿的凯尔·C的另一个粉丝提问，

961
