1732
01:12:03.160 --> 01:12:05.420
I live for our Miles McNutt reviews.
我就是靠着听迈尔斯的剧评过活的。

1733
01:12:05.420 --> 01:12:14.760
Well, Miles actually stopped writing reviews for The Office at the end of Season 8, but the new reviewer was out this week, the week of Roy's wedding.
好吧，迈尔斯其实在第八季结束时就不再为《办公室》写剧评了，但新剧评人这周，也就是罗伊婚礼的那周，没有出稿。

1734
01:12:15.000 --> 01:12:16.660
So Miles wrote this review.
所以迈尔斯写了这篇剧评。

1735
01:12:16.660 --> 01:12:19.460
This was his final review of The Office.
这是他对《办公室》的最后一篇剧评。

1736
01:12:19.880 --> 01:12:29.520
He gave this episode a B, and he reviewed this episode, but he also kind of gave some thoughts about the new direction of Season 9, which he was liking very much.
他给这一集打了B，并且他不仅评了这一集，还对第九季的新方向发表了一些看法，他非常喜欢这个新方向。

1737
01:12:29.680 --> 01:12:32.040
For example, he loves Jerk Andy.
比如，他超爱混蛋安迪。

1738
01:12:32.640 --> 01:12:33.180
Okay.
好吧。

1739
01:12:33.180 --> 01:12:34.420
He liked that change.
他很喜欢这个转变。

1740
01:12:34.560 --> 01:12:39.100
He likes the addition of Clark and Pete, and he loved the Jim-Pam storyline.
他喜欢克拉克和皮特的加入，并且他超爱吉姆和帕姆的故事线。

1741
01:12:39.620 --> 01:12:41.200
Here's what he said, quote,
他是这么说的，引述如下：

1742
01:12:41.700 --> 01:12:49.440
It's the couple's strongest storyline in a long time, and it's also giving the show the kind of arc structure that it lacked last season.
这是这对情侣很长一段时间以来最强的剧情线，这也为剧集带来了上季所缺乏的那种宏大故事结构。

1743
01:12:49.660 --> 01:12:59.100
Heck, it's even retroactively giving last season meaning, with Jim and Pam's boring storylines now becoming a period within their larger arc,
见鬼，它甚至追溯性地赋予了上一季意义，吉姆和帕姆那些无聊的剧情线现在成了他们宏大故事弧中的一个阶段，

1744
01:12:59.100 --> 01:13:07.280
which was underserved and often outright ignored in Season 8, which I actually thought was such a good point.
而这在第八季中着墨不多，甚至常常被直接忽略，我觉得这个观点真的太棒了。

1745
01:13:07.460 --> 01:13:19.260
We barely checked in on Jim and Pam's relationship in Season 8, and now this idea that their relationship was too boring to check in on is becoming a major story point.
我们在第八季里几乎没怎么关注吉姆和帕姆的关系，现在这种“他们的关系无聊到不值得关注”的想法成了一个主要的剧情点。

1746
01:13:19.260 --> 01:13:21.980
So genius of Greg to think of this.
格雷格能想到这一点简直太天才了。

1747
01:13:21.980 --> 01:13:23.420
He went on to say,
他接着说道：

1748
01:13:56.920 --> 01:13:57.360
Wow.
哇。

1749
01:13:58.360 --> 01:14:07.740
I think that I had to read that because I'm really, really proud because John and I got to be a part of crafting this, and Greg really listened to us,
我想我必须读读这段，因为我真的、真的很骄傲，因为约翰和我参与了构思这个过程，而且格雷格真的听取了我们的意见，

1750
01:14:07.800 --> 01:14:12.440
and we wanted all the things that he just said to land on the audience, so I was so happy.
我们希望他刚才说的那些点都能真正触动观众，所以我真的超级开心。

1751
01:14:12.440 --> 01:14:14.940
Also, Miles is such a good writer.
另外，迈尔斯真的是个好作家。

1752
01:14:15.120 --> 01:14:15.960
Can we just say that?
我们可以直接这么说吗？

1753
01:14:16.020 --> 01:14:16.200
I know.
我懂的。

1754
01:14:16.200 --> 01:14:18.940
Like, everything he wrote there, I was like, yes!
就好像他写的所有东西，我都觉得：对！

1755
01:14:19.280 --> 01:14:19.900
I know.
我懂的。

1756
01:14:20.080 --> 01:14:22.780
Kind of opened up to how I'm looking at the season now.
这有点启发了我现在看待这一季的方式。

1757
01:14:23.080 --> 01:14:24.800
I felt so seen when I read it.
我读到的时候觉得深有同感。

1758
01:14:25.100 --> 01:14:28.160
And then also, Miles signed off in this way.
然后还有，迈尔斯最后是这样署名的。

1759
01:14:28.180 --> 01:14:29.000
He said,
他说：

1760
01:14:29.180 --> 01:14:35.220
An earnest thank you to everyone who has read or commented on my review of the show over the past two years.
衷心感谢过去两年里所有阅读或评论我该剧剧评的朋友们。

1761
01:14:35.320 --> 01:14:41.680
It's been incredibly rewarding and enjoyable to go head-to-head about a show that people connect with so personally
能和一部让大家产生如此深厚的情感共鸣

1762
01:14:41.680 --> 01:14:43.520
and have strong opinions about.
且有着强烈看法的剧集针锋相对，这段经历极其充实且令人愉快。

1763
01:14:43.720 --> 01:14:48.680
And I'll admit that I'll likely be dropping in and out of the comments as the season goes on.
我也承认，随着这一季的播出，我大概还是会时不时在评论区露面。

1764
01:14:49.180 --> 01:14:52.440
However, I do so not as a critic but as a viewer.
不过，我不再以评论员的身份，而是以观众的身份这么做。

1765
01:14:52.580 --> 01:14:58.560
So do feel free to insult my person as you would any other commenter with whom you strongly disagree.
所以，大家完全可以像对待任何其他你强烈反对的评论员那样，尽管来人身攻击我。

1766
01:14:58.980 --> 01:15:00.200
It's only fair.
这很公平。

1767
01:15:01.360 --> 01:15:04.100
Aw, Miles, we're going to miss your reviews.
噢，迈尔斯，我们会想念你的剧评的。

1768
01:15:04.420 --> 01:15:07.860
Yes, Miles, you have made this rewatch so enjoyable.
是的，迈尔斯，你让这次重温变得如此愉快。

1769
01:15:08.000 --> 01:15:11.420
I've loved your insight and your thoughts.
我太喜欢你的见解和想法了。

1770
01:15:12.020 --> 01:15:18.340
I'm sad that we won't have any of your reviews for Dwight and Angela's rekindling.
一想到德怀特和安吉拉重修旧好时再也看不到你的剧评，我就很难过。

1771
01:15:18.580 --> 01:15:22.520
And I would have loved to have seen your reviews on the Senator and Oscar.
而且我也很想看到你对参议员和奥斯卡的评价。

1772
01:15:22.940 --> 01:15:28.060
Yes, Angela, that storyline is not in this episode and he didn't comment on it.
对啦，安吉拉，这一集里没有那个故事情节，而且他也没有对此发表评论。

1773
01:15:28.140 --> 01:15:31.480
But I have to believe that he loved it as much as we do.
但我坚信他肯定和我们一样喜欢这个情节。

1774
01:15:31.760 --> 01:15:34.300
Or would have had some very interesting thoughts.
或者说他本会有很多非常有趣的看法。

1775
01:15:34.320 --> 01:15:35.660
I welcome either.
这两种我都欢迎。

1776
01:15:36.220 --> 01:15:38.960
Maybe I'll have to check the comments as we go along.
也许随着剧情推进，我得去评论区看看了。

1777
01:15:38.960 --> 01:15:39.840
Oh, yes.
噢，是的。

1778
01:15:40.240 --> 01:15:42.340
Miles, we might look for you in the comments.
迈尔斯，我们可能会在评论区找你哦。

1779
01:15:42.520 --> 01:15:42.660
Yep.
没错。

1780
01:15:42.960 --> 01:15:44.900
See if Miles is there and Steve B.
看看迈尔斯和史蒂夫·B在不在。

1781
01:15:45.220 --> 01:15:46.300
Yeah, that's right.
对，没错。

1782
01:15:46.540 --> 01:15:47.080
Steve B.
史蒂夫·B。

1783
01:15:47.300 --> 01:15:48.040
a.k.a.
也就是

1784
01:15:48.300 --> 01:15:49.180
Steve Burgess.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯。

1785
01:15:49.240 --> 01:15:50.200
Or so we think.
或者我们以为是。

1786
01:15:51.160 --> 01:15:52.140
Defending the show.
捍卫这部剧。

1787
01:15:52.140 --> 01:16:02.020
Well, now Daryl and Andy are going to call a voluntary meeting in the conference room to discuss Erin's confidence, but also like her body.
好了，现在达里尔和安迪要在会议室召开一次自愿会议，来讨论艾琳的自信，但也包括她的身材之类的。

1788
01:16:02.200 --> 01:16:04.040
Basically her outward appearance.
基本上就是她的外表。

1789
01:16:04.200 --> 01:16:04.460
Yes.
是的。

1790
01:16:04.460 --> 01:16:09.940
Because once again, I guess in order to be a newscaster, you just, it's all about your looks.
因为又一次，我猜要想当个新闻主播，你只需要……这完全取决于你的外表。

1791
01:16:10.520 --> 01:16:13.060
Doesn't matter about your journalism degree.
新闻学学位根本不重要。

1792
01:16:13.580 --> 01:16:16.140
Not for this news job.
这份新闻工作不需要。

1793
01:16:16.280 --> 01:16:17.020
That's right.
没错。

1794
01:16:17.040 --> 01:16:25.080
We also are going to learn in a Daryl talking head that he has become Andy's conciliary, or also known as the assistant regional manager.
我们还将在达里尔的单独访谈中得知，他已经成了安迪的顾问，也就是大家所说的助理分公司经理。

1795
01:16:25.400 --> 01:16:25.980
Yeah.
对。

1796
01:16:26.560 --> 01:16:34.940
So I want you guys to know, Daryl is going to be part of several scenes with Andy and Erin as they figure out how she's going to be a news anchor.
所以我想让大家知道，当安迪和艾琳在琢磨她该如何成为一名新闻主播时，达里尔将会参与其中的好几场戏。

1797
01:16:35.400 --> 01:16:37.140
There's a bunch of deleted scenes, too.
还有一堆被删减的片段呢。

1798
01:16:37.240 --> 01:16:38.440
I'll share them when they come up.
等它们出现时我会分享出来的。

1799
01:16:38.660 --> 01:16:44.100
Well, when this conference room begins, there's an interesting moment, and we got a fan question about it, from Kaylee F.
好了，当这个会议开始时，有一个有趣的时刻，我们收到了一个关于它的粉丝提问，来自夏威夷的

1800
01:16:44.240 --> 01:16:44.640
in Hawaii.
凯莉·F。

1801
01:16:44.640 --> 01:16:46.500
I hope I'm pronouncing your name correctly.
希望我没有把你的名字念错。

1802
01:16:46.760 --> 01:16:53.800
Who said, Angela, what are you saying to Oscar in the conference room when Andy reveals Erin's pursuit of an anchor person audition?
安吉拉，当安迪透露艾琳在争取主播试镜时，你在会议室里对奥斯卡说了什么？

1803
01:16:53.820 --> 01:16:57.060
It seems a little out of character that you're just chatting with your friend.
你们俩只是在闲聊，这感觉有点不符合你们的人设。

1804
01:16:58.040 --> 01:16:59.740
This is such a great catch.
这个发现真是太棒了。

1805
01:17:00.020 --> 01:17:10.540
So in the shooting draft, Angela and Oscar had a lot of back and forth comments about Erin being a news anchor, and they seemed to really bond over being judgy about it.
所以在拍摄剧本里，安吉拉和奥斯卡有很多关于艾琳当新闻主播的来回评论，他们似乎真的因为一起对此评头论足而拉近了距离。

1806
01:17:10.760 --> 01:17:12.260
Some of it made deleted scenes.
其中一部分被剪成了删减片段。

1807
01:17:12.420 --> 01:17:12.940
Let's hear it.
我们听听看。

1808
01:17:13.380 --> 01:17:14.980
Does Erin have any experience?
艾琳有什么经验吗？

1809
01:17:15.300 --> 01:17:17.300
Has she taken any journalism classes, maybe?
她上过什么新闻学课程吗？

1810
01:17:17.640 --> 01:17:19.020
Has she done the pageant circuit?
她参加过选美比赛吗？

1811
01:17:19.500 --> 01:17:20.480
I watched the news.
我看过新闻。

1812
01:17:20.500 --> 01:17:21.940
She's going to be amazing.
她会表现得非常棒。

1813
01:17:21.940 --> 01:17:22.520
Look at her.
看看她。

1814
01:17:22.640 --> 01:17:23.660
She's going to light up the screen.
她会点亮荧幕的。

1815
01:17:23.940 --> 01:17:25.100
Does she even want to do it?
她自己甚至想做这个吗？

1816
01:17:25.380 --> 01:17:26.480
Of course she wants to do it.
她当然想做这个。

1817
01:17:26.500 --> 01:17:27.460
She answers phones.
她只是个接线员。

1818
01:17:27.980 --> 01:17:29.160
That's not fair, Angela.
这不公平，安吉拉。

1819
01:17:29.460 --> 01:17:31.020
Some people don't aspire for anything.
有些人没有什么远大抱负。

1820
01:17:31.240 --> 01:17:32.180
Erin, that's just fine forever.
艾琳，那样永远也挺好的。

1821
01:17:32.700 --> 01:17:32.960
Hey.
嘿。

1822
01:17:33.340 --> 01:17:33.780
Hey.
嘿。

1823
01:17:34.020 --> 01:17:34.720
Over here.
看这里。

1824
01:17:35.900 --> 01:17:41.480
So what happens is, when they were trimming the scene, some of this back and forth got trimmed,
所以情况是这样的，他们在精简这场戏时，这些来回对话被剪掉了一些，

1825
01:17:41.480 --> 01:17:46.820
but the end of it is there where Oscar and I are kind of leaning over, and he's like, Angela, that's not fair.
但结尾还在，奥斯卡和我凑过去，他好像在说，安吉拉，这不公平。

1826
01:17:46.900 --> 01:17:47.720
And I'm like, okay, fine.
然后我说，好吧，行吧。

1827
01:17:47.800 --> 01:17:48.540
Well, if you say so.
好吧，如果你这么说的话。

1828
01:17:49.260 --> 01:17:51.340
And we're having our little hubbub, hubbub, hubbub.
然后我们在那里叽叽喳喳、议论个不停。

1829
01:17:51.640 --> 01:17:51.920
Okay.
好吧。

1830
01:17:51.920 --> 01:17:55.560
And then Erin is meant to interrupt us and say, hey, over here.
然后艾琳本该打断我们并说，嘿，看这里。

1831
01:17:55.800 --> 01:17:57.140
I want to do this.
我想做这个。

1832
01:17:57.260 --> 01:17:59.760
So you're catching us having this little hubbub.
所以你们看到我们在那里议论纷纷。

1833
01:18:00.100 --> 01:18:02.580
But Oscar and I were such longtime friends.
但奥斯卡和我一直是老朋友。

1834
01:18:02.760 --> 01:18:04.680
You know, we had met years before the office.
你知道的，我们在《办公室》开拍多年前就认识了。

1835
01:18:04.680 --> 01:18:05.480
I've shared this.
我已经分享过这个了。

1836
01:18:05.620 --> 01:18:07.880
We had performed in sketch comedy together.
我们曾一起表演过素描喜剧。

1837
01:18:08.280 --> 01:18:12.680
We were so giddy about having any kind of storyline together.
能有任何形式的共同剧情，我们都兴奋得不得了。

1838
01:18:13.900 --> 01:18:17.020
And this season in particular, we get to have a lot.
特别是这一季，我们有很多对手戏。

1839
01:18:17.020 --> 01:18:25.400
So a lot of that, I do think you see the friendship that's there that maybe Angela and Oscar didn't have to the extent that we had in real life.
所以我觉得在很多地方，你能看出那种友谊的存在，这种友谊可能安吉拉和奥斯卡在现实中并没有我们那么深厚。

1840
01:18:25.700 --> 01:18:33.160
Andy is now going to ask everyone to name something they like about Erin's body so that she can feel more confident about her audition.
安迪现在要让每个人说出他们喜欢艾琳身体的哪个部位，这样她就能对试镜更有信心。

1841
01:18:33.560 --> 01:18:35.340
Daryl says he likes her hair.
达里尔说他喜欢她的头发。

1842
01:18:35.740 --> 01:18:38.960
Andy says that attractive people appear more trustworthy.
安迪说有吸引力的人显得更值得信赖。

1843
01:18:38.960 --> 01:18:45.080
And Oscar is going to object and kind of bring up Walter Cronkite's reign as the most trusted man in America.
然后奥斯卡会反驳，并顺便提到了沃尔特·克朗凯特作为美国最值得信赖之人的统治地位。

1844
01:18:45.420 --> 01:18:51.600
And then Meredith is going to say she thought Walter Cronkite was hot and would take that mustache ride.
然后梅雷迪思会说她觉得沃尔特·克朗凯特很性感，愿意跟他那撮小胡子风流快活一番。

1845
01:18:51.840 --> 01:18:54.040
Go to 15 minutes and 56 seconds.
快进到15分56秒处。

1846
01:18:54.820 --> 01:18:55.760
What will I see?
我会看到什么？

1847
01:18:56.380 --> 01:19:03.600
You will see Angela Martin making a face, Jim making a face, and Creed looking inquisitive slash making a face.
你会看到安吉拉·马丁做了一个鬼脸，吉姆做了一个鬼脸，而克里德看起来很好奇或者说做了一个鬼脸。

1848
01:19:04.080 --> 01:19:05.940
I took a screen grab of it.
我截了张图。

1849
01:19:06.020 --> 01:19:06.920
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

1850
01:19:07.560 --> 01:19:08.520
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1851
01:19:08.960 --> 01:19:13.300
Erin is going to do a mock reading for Daryl and Andy.
艾琳要为达里尔和安迪进行模拟播报。

1852
01:19:13.560 --> 01:19:17.900
She has written her news copy, and it doesn't make any sense.
她写好了新闻稿，但完全不知所云。

1853
01:19:18.160 --> 01:19:26.000
But the thing that they are going to give her a note about is how long she pauses between saying,
不过他们要给她提出意见的地方，是她在说完

1854
01:19:26.300 --> 01:19:30.740
for Channel 11 News, I'm Erin Hannon.
我是11频道新闻的艾琳·汉农。这句台词之间停顿了多久。

1855
01:19:31.060 --> 01:19:32.520
No, longer pause.
不，停顿再长一点。

1856
01:19:32.800 --> 01:19:33.640
Even longer.
还要更长。

1857
01:19:33.900 --> 01:19:35.120
It's going to build suspense.
这样才能营造悬念。

1858
01:19:35.120 --> 01:19:36.160
Don't be shy.
别害羞。

1859
01:19:37.140 --> 01:19:43.600
There are more scenes of Andy working with Erin while Daryl, oh, poor Daryl, has to sit there and watch this.
还有更多安迪指导艾琳的场景，而达里尔——噢，可怜的达里尔——只能坐在那里看着。

1860
01:19:44.560 --> 01:19:46.000
Here's one I need you to hear.
这里有一段我需要你听听看。

1861
01:19:47.280 --> 01:19:49.120
But I'm really bad at public speaking.
但我很不擅长公开演讲。

1862
01:19:49.560 --> 01:19:51.140
Don't think of it as public speaking.
别把它当成公开演讲。

1863
01:19:51.280 --> 01:19:52.600
Think of it as music.
把它当成音乐。

1864
01:19:52.780 --> 01:19:54.280
The news is music.
新闻就是音乐。

1865
01:19:54.540 --> 01:19:55.280
You sing it.
你把它唱出来。

1866
01:19:55.280 --> 01:19:57.680
Ma-ma-ma-ma-ma-ma-ma-ma-ma.
玛——玛——玛——玛——玛——玛——玛——玛——玛。

1867
01:19:57.680 --> 01:19:58.980
